  "review_scope": "Two actual Jev examples per source; complete schema/group checks and original-file comparisons where recorded. Not an audit of every label.",
  "findings": {
    "newsmtsc": "Author framing includes implicit attitudes conveyed by reported actions; the prompt asks how the author portrays the marked target. Official rw converted Parquet; no duplicate mt training view.",
    "sentihood": "All distinct train/test opinions match original JSON. Original dev ID 306 has conflicting Positive/Negative safety opinions; Hub silently retains Positive. Exclude it before flattening. Emit only native Positive/Negative opinions; unannotated aspects never become neutral or synthetic negatives.",
    "mams": "Every train/dev/test sentence and ordered term/polarity pair exactly matches original ATSA XML. Generation instructions and their example answers never enter model inputs.",
    "uk-election": "Native archive join is reproducible and split-ID offset is validated bijectively. Coarse review nevertheless found negative VAT with no supporting sentiment in a list of topics, and uncertain positive crime under sarcastic Maybe not. Park training, retain native mirror and evidence for future review."
  },
